  "id": "DrugBank_DB08904 - MONDO_grouped_7126_8468_24512_13192",
  "verbalization": "Certolizumab Pegol, an anti-TNF inhibitor, is associated with Ankylosing Spondylitis (AS), a condition linked to Spondyloarthropathy, Susceptibility To. This relationship is supported by its indirect pathway through Ixekizumab and Golimumab, both of which are also indicated for AS. The evidence suggests that Certolizumab Pegol may influence the pathophysiology of AS by modulating inflammatory processes, potentially enhancing the immune response against the disease. The shared indication for AS among these drugs implies a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the inhibition of TNF-alpha or similar inflammatory mediators. The cumulative evidence points to a role for Certolizumab Pegol in the development or progression of Spondyloarthropathy, Susceptibility To, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
